[{"id":"VRCE-2-63-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":1,"english":"The very same night that the envoys entered the city, Bharata saw an evil dream.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19e9137e9f3a5d8227ab1ede818f4954150fb101187ca0a109e8e9daabd91859","compact":"3066d83fefa2b06a832dc82c103344c16f7a70af34a6d4f994f83d01f1e9519f","nasal":"e55066e6fb90ee572411f7d27bf90a626998677d21e8a9533a8aa2814d7acaa7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":2,"english":"And seeing that evil dream during the short hours, the son of that king of kings exceedingly burned in grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb4bf395349daddc2e6e5ccc066bcbc8ad8fac2f6c50318c96da643c04262448","compact":"0b9060bbb2d498f7947f8ede37dde2747c3fef7c6623c75c6476c541b83a76b8","nasal":"b3b65a9e26ebd701d27f61ed428666db75c3b27c0c65aa77c3a1d3200c3b8666"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":3,"english":"And finding him aggrieved, his sweet. speeched associates, endeavouring to chase the heaviness, began to converse on a variety of subjects.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"81736e8e5ffe195285fa86bde1f8d9e2f901d013e61329bcf173d201582a9114","compact":"fa82116f1e28a2067f783d12a2a75f7c3a24011b2e6bb061984b9e1ca7aa6826","nasal":"e3471f90f3b1f1badfa8dafde5200a0015d18c386e648e065e259edcadc04521"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":4,"english":"Some played on instruments; some for the purpose of pacifying his mind, danced (the courtezans); others performed scenes variously fraught with the sentiment of mirth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.587,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6110a56431c7352ff9b8e587e64f311f3ba848a17369de7f2dba614338e327c7","compact":"240ede26b79ac6b423ae59bcdcec97adc66a8baaefe7f086e7ef47252e5dcd63","nasal":"d83c81796c33891abccf376ac11b95033ff2109176fe3e0bd30a0cf9c3f3953d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":5,"english":"But although his friends intending to ally his agitation set about enacting passages calculated to amuse family circles, that magnanimous descendant of Raghu did not indulge in laughter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"575beb022fdfeaa2b3ecf322f9489d477cf6bde6e2c442754d80e70e777149a3","compact":"d86d0cdb90ebb933135ddafce6c056cb94f597c0522f5ceb64138597731ad9e3","nasal":"d86d0cdb90ebb933135ddafce6c056cb94f597c0522f5ceb64138597731ad9e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":6,"english":"Then a dear friend addressed Bharata, as he sat surrounded by his friends, “Surrounded by your friends, why do you not, my friend, join in the mirth?\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1972a56d51b4a75df9a72700c26764b42fbbf358ea101cd97c547767c3e8340","compact":"641df94720e744e9492959dbdd18ff420b848ff511896c9c5ea3ee4dbefa20d6","nasal":"641df94720e744e9492959dbdd18ff420b848ff511896c9c5ea3ee4dbefa20d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":7,"english":"Thus asked by his friend, Bharata answered, “Listen why this depression has overtaken me. In a dream I beheld my father, pale, with his hair loosely flowing about, plunging from the summit of a mountain into a dirty pool filled with cowdung.”","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3682428242ec788fef6deaa2839ddeb79fd4246dc602ca8343d7be10f3d0051e","compact":"9c778f1939c843d39cd57bf6bd0d0f6933441b78bc019928816311c3864b54e6","nasal":"a8b75ccd69fb0e66339567057093aa6f6cf29e4a2e5a95f90a135d2695150172"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":8,"english":"Thus asked by his friend, Bharata answered, “Listen why this depression has overtaken me. In a dream I beheld my father, pale, with his hair loosely flowing about, plunging from the summit of a mountain into a dirty pool filled with cowdung.”","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.937,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eaa06380e7c71acfb608551e788e35cdc25c822aeba17ad7687ef80fb6124f9a","compact":"313fc4cc919c4664a22b03b037a424dd029cf7d0e43f3f2645cf617bd067edc9","nasal":"f344be54947a8b4383b49571699a61376cdbdb64fadac2a99555ec26db45cab2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":9,"english":"And I saw him floating on a sink of cowdung, and yet with a momentary laugh drinking oil by means of his joined hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53cf4eac013b083f13a2ba2010c77b8afb387abe852f5c258857105d3eebd5ac","compact":"2fa67fcb8c6a8164495ada7c8c33e6f2fe3ed5cd2b0db29b1ab341cb17adc91c","nasal":"dc960c1ac49541b8dc873b4fc5f9209fd331fbb2d1feba1ffc1eccc509e00533"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":10,"english":"Then feeding on rice mixed with sesame, he again and again hanging his head down, dives into oil with his limbs rubbed with oil.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.918,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd3f370a75f626781c4d55f574229668cf70da0803f58037bc065caaf9f061f4","compact":"a00dd4bfc98fa9ae9a2b37759592e7b2e00b13e5bf0b5e5a6474c51bca7af34d","nasal":"21ebd6bfe93b769cc36f568174e3f5550d32323be76acc0c5e091375a68c2dc1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":11,"english":"And in my dream I saw the ocean dried up, and the moon fallen on the earth, and the earth as if invaded by enfolding darkness, and the tusk of the elephant on which the monarch rides falling in fragments, and flaming fire suddenly extinguished, and the earth rent, and the trees withered, and all the mountains belching smoke.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.557,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"510575ced08363c70a1efe46eb0634ce24759a117315ca8054ec0312e423f40e","compact":"318890b54fc07d0b0cba37ebad3865c772a9a18524bf5f02037012ae124f83f2","nasal":"ebbad92767a58a2fd2aab10c2caece26f2087bda476dcb58d71a3b0dcd9b4a86"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":12,"english":"And in my dream I saw the ocean dried up, and the moon fallen on the earth, and the earth as if invaded by enfolding darkness, and the tusk of the elephant on which the monarch rides falling in fragments, and flaming fire suddenly extinguished, and the earth rent, and the trees withered, and all the mountains belching smoke.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.779,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dbc0e326c35562f534e721f4317e88a6a7265e33c6885f37ecef5a73061eac68","compact":"d29d39a18b993ab6ae7034b64042495210dce7dbfc6a00180608c2d5f5192505","nasal":"bae3d00b81e77591d25ee3729d298423eae593867a6812823e8647b2db94c348"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":13,"english":"I saw the king seated on a sable seat of iron, clad in a sable garb; and women black and yellow beating him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.632,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"329d81fcd02ac226e858b06b17ba63b9b55b8d5a1a8c92895fa4b6e3bf9d016e","compact":"1d6a99d9660b9c8c36ca9225a8e5c05fcc32a6460ddf2e1ca7ca3e6e21f30160","nasal":"505a94fe72bfee6648d858b6dd5ab24ebaf315b064786ee5b7de0eceb7f92e4c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":14,"english":"And bearing a garland of red flowers, with his body daubed with red sandal, he was fast proceeding to the south in a car yoked with asses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f7cb07c008c2506d8109af2fe01f36696a42e5834da237539f3630e7f09a71c3","compact":"b4ec1ef69cdc36ae8af7fcbd2a36e31c32a9a6609c6c42314bf080f1f0094330","nasal":"b4ec1ef69cdc36ae8af7fcbd2a36e31c32a9a6609c6c42314bf080f1f0094330"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":15,"english":"This was the dream that I saw this terrible night. Either I, or Rama, or the king, or Lakşmaņa is to breathe our last.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5746939bd1263d306f63a69233000bfc3459ea4b7103edfe60e926ad6b190eb","compact":"bedc5357eaebd82dcde6d443f8866ebf379c4b471f132205153e02de99af1da1","nasal":"bedc5357eaebd82dcde6d443f8866ebf379c4b471f132205153e02de99af1da1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":16,"english":"The smoke of the funeral pyre of him will be shortly visible that goes in the car yoked with asses. It is for this reason that I am poor of spirit, and that I do not respond to your words. Further, my throat is parched, and my mind ill at ease.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.722,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8cc90225e14c1a162f08c742cd96f4fc3dba89113f24db6fd3e2d160583e7bf8","compact":"bf4509540fb9ecde29a6665e63638b806eebe01491d4aaad91a9923f95a24c46","nasal":"b5c4df3129af7712c2b38f8bde8b72d76ff496f32cd621601d8f12680597ea81"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":17,"english":"The smoke of the funeral pyre of him will be shortly visible that goes in the car yoked with asses. It is for this reason that I am poor of spirit, and that I do not respond to your words. Further, my throat is parched, and my mind ill at ease. Ground of fear find I none, yet am I subject to fear. My voice is untuned, and my grace fled, and I begin to despise my life, nor know I the reason why.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.407,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-15","DUTT-2-69-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f341401921d482df2e1c50dfc7b4cee8bcb8d9f53bdf5d37c5f9adac9a9711d","compact":"28c36de25223ce7837e6fbce0087c250d2875813781da9ee0eabce2a09b7fe05","nasal":"f6008e0f44130d49ed2b38a2060faea9e59a99cc44e86dfa71e740752bb38e75"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-63-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":63,"verse":18,"english":"Bringing to mind this various-looking dream which I had not thought of before, and remembering the king of incomprehensible presence, this fear goes not from my heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.619,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-69-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2063018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc1d2e8bb9fb2e6752a244230b149b33953b5a2d5626830f3f31262f4401d893","compact":"b364f5d65c4df31e0d73bfdfcd1fb1b0829985f19d9d5859ee21e5ed4e91eef8","nasal":"6f64ebe36e517039a0101e5039ba87d6b01b6cdc598ddc8fb3bfe30f0265f3a3"}}]
